### Login como ADMIN (guarda o token na variável "token"). Requer um usuário ADMIN já existente no banco
@admin_email = admin@example.com
@admin_password = change-me-123
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{admin_email}}",
  "password": "{{admin_password}}"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("token", response.body.token);
%}

### Criar ANALYST com UFs de cobertura (guarda o id em "analyst_id") -> 201
POST {{host}}/admin/users
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "email": "analyst@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "role": "ANALYST",
  "coverageUfs": [
    "SP",
    "DF"
  ]
}

> {%
    client.global.set("analyst_id", response.body.id);
%}

### Criar ANALYST sem UFs -> 400
POST {{host}}/admin/users
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "email": "analyst-sem-uf@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "role": "ANALYST"
}

### Criar ADMIN (guarda o id em "admin2_id") -> 201
POST {{host}}/admin/users
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "email": "admin2@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "role": "ADMIN"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("admin2_id", response.body.id);
%}

### Criar ADMIN com UFs -> 400
POST {{host}}/admin/users
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "email": "admin3@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "role": "ADMIN",
  "coverageUfs": [
    "SP"
  ]
}

### Criar com role CLIENT -> 400
POST {{host}}/admin/users
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "email": "client@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "role": "CLIENT"
}

### Sem token -> 401
POST {{host}}/admin/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "x@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "role": "ANALYST"
}

### Atualizar cobertura do ANALYST (substitui a lista inteira; requer token ADMIN) -> 200
PUT {{host}}/admin/users/{{analyst_id}}/coverage
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "coverageUfs": [
    "RJ",
    "MG"
  ]
}

### Atualizar cobertura com lista vazia -> 400
PUT {{host}}/admin/users/{{analyst_id}}/coverage
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "coverageUfs": []
}

### Atualizar cobertura sem o campo -> 400
PUT {{host}}/admin/users/{{analyst_id}}/coverage
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{}

### Atualizar cobertura com UF inválida -> 400
PUT {{host}}/admin/users/{{analyst_id}}/coverage
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "coverageUfs": [
    "XX"
  ]
}

### Atualizar cobertura de um ADMIN -> 400
PUT {{host}}/admin/users/{{admin2_id}}/coverage
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "coverageUfs": [
    "SP"
  ]
}

### Atualizar cobertura de usuário inexistente -> 404
PUT {{host}}/admin/users/999999/coverage
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "coverageUfs": [
    "SP"
  ]
}

### Atualizar cobertura sem token -> 401
PUT {{host}}/admin/users/{{analyst_id}}/coverage
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "coverageUfs": [
    "SP"
  ]
}



### Login (guarda o token na variável "token") -- com analista
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "analyst@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("token", response.body.token);
%}
